<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.6 bln in Jan 27 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.6 bln in Jan 27 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.6 billion in the January 27 week to $3,857.8 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $9.5 billion to $4,978.9 billion. M-1 fell $7.4 billion to $1,084.1 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,850.3 billion versus $3,844.8 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
